<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.7">
  <!--
    Transparent plastic cup used as a place target. Built from primitives, not
    a mesh, for the same reason tube_rack is: get_location_profile() in
    simulate.py derives floor_height / is_container by scanning collisions for
    box and cylinder geometry, and returns is_container=False for anything
    mesh-based. A mesh location therefore always falls back to the "hover
    above the rim and let go" branch, which is what every non-rack location in
    this folder used to do.

    Measured on the physical cup: base 55 mm outside diameter,
    mouth 80 mm. HEIGHT IS NOT A MEASURED VALUE — 120 mm is a
    plausible figure for a cup with those two diameters. Measure the real one
    and change H below; nothing else in the file needs to move, and nothing in
    the backend hard-codes this height (resolve_location_metrics reads the SDF).

    Geometry: 12 tapered wall panels approximating a truncated cone, half-angle
    5.95 deg, panel slant length 120.6 mm. The floor is a
    square plate inscribed in the base circle rather than a cylinder, because
    only a BOX collision can be recognized as the container floor — a cylinder
    contributes to the rim height and nothing else. A tube is placed at the
    cup's centre, so the square's smaller footprint is not a constraint.

    Chosen over the Google Scanned Objects mug that used to occupy this folder,
    which was a non-static mesh: it drifted under physics and offered no
    container semantics.
  -->
  <model name="cup">
    <static>true</static>

    <link name="link">

      <!-- Container floor. Must be a box, and must stay thin relative to its
           own width (the detector requires size_z < min(size_x, size_y) / 2),
           or the cup stops reading as a container. -->
      <collision name="col_floor">
        <pose>0 0 0.00100 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.03811 0.03811 0.00200</size></box></geometry>
        <surface><friction><ode><mu>0.9</mu><mu2>0.9</mu2></ode></friction></surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name="vis_floor">
        <pose>0 0 0.00100 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.02750</radius><length>0.00200</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.70 0.78 0.85 0.45</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.70 0.78 0.85 0.45</diffuse>
        </material>
        <transparency>0.55</transparency>
      </visual>

      <collision name="col_wall_0">
        <pose>0.03375 0.00000 0.06000 0 0.10379 0.00000</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.00200 0.01953 0.12065</size></box></geometry>
        <surface><friction><ode><mu>0.9</mu><mu2>0.9</mu2></ode></friction></surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name="vis_wall_0">
